<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Agrippa II</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 27–c. 93</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century">1st century</a> · Also known as Herod Agrippa II, Marcus Julius Agrippa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Agrippa II was the last ruler of the Herodian dynasty, son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herod-agrippa-i">Herod Agrippa I</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> gave him the kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chalcis">Chalcis</a> in about 50 and later larger territories in the north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palestine">Palestine</a>. He sided with Rome in the Jewish revolt of 66 to 70, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acts-of-the-apostles">Acts of the Apostles</a> records him hearing the apostle Paul at Caesarea.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/agrippa-ii.jpg" alt="Agrippa II" width="320" height="154" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CNG · CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Agrippa_II_Judaea_Capta_91000679.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
